# Call-site ledger of asyncstdlib at 0c5e206189e20466bae9468f13be7f3d49fa70a5 (v3.14.0).
# Hand-written from the source; judgements in asyncstdlib.md.
#
# Roles: the package values that can reach a parameter (asyncstdlib.md, "Roles").
#   Iterable role: every parameter documented as an (async) iterable (AnyIterable,
#     AsyncIterable, AsyncIterator). Package values: the async generators of the
#     package's async generator functions and expressions, and the async iterator
#     objects TeePeer, chain, GroupBy, _Grouper, _BorrowedAsyncIterator and
#     _ScopedAsyncIterator (docs/source/notes/iter_scope.rst; the package and the
#     tests pass them). A Tee is not a value of this role. aiter() of such a value
#     returns the value itself.
#   An async for over such a value runs TeePeer.__aiter__ or
#     _BorrowedAsyncIterator.__aiter__ (also for _ScopedAsyncIterator), and the
#     __anext__ of TeePeer, chain, GroupBy or _Grouper. chain, GroupBy and _Grouper
#     inherit collections.abc.AsyncIterator.__aiter__, and the borrowed and scoped
#     iterators forward __anext__ to an async generator: code outside the package,
#     no edge at an implicit site.
#   Async context manager role: NullContext, _AsyncGeneratorContextManager and
#     _ScopedAsyncIteratorContext (the package classes that subclass
#     AsyncContextManager), and what the package passes itself (NoLock).
#   Callable roles (function, key, predicate, callback): no package value, except
#     the defaults (itertools.add, itertools.identity, heapq._identity, bool) and
#     ExitStack.enter_context, which a test passes to map.
#   Awaitable role: no package value.
default reject asyncstdlib.itertools.Tee.__getitem__: no package code subscripts a Tee, and none iterates, unpacks or searches one (Tee defines __iter__, so iteration never falls back to __getitem__); the subscripted objects are typing constructs in annotations, tuples, lists, dicts, OrderedDicts, instance __dict__s, the sys.exc_info() tuple and the list nodes of the tee buffer
default reject asyncstdlib.itertools.Tee.__iter__, asyncstdlib.itertools.Tee.__len__: no package code iterates, unpacks, converts, measures or truth-tests a Tee; a Tee is not a value of the iterable role (header; asyncstdlib.md, "Roles"), and the package keeps no Tee of its own
default reject asyncstdlib._lrucache.CallKey.__eq__, asyncstdlib._lrucache.CallKey.__hash__: a CallKey exists only as a key of the dict or OrderedDict of MemoizedLRUAsyncCallable and CachedLRUAsyncCallable; only the dict operations of their __call__ and cache_discard hash and compare it (accepted there); every other hashed or compared value is a str, int, tuple, type, sentinel, typing construct or client value
default reject asyncstdlib.heapq._KeyIter.__eq__: two _KeyIter objects are compared only inside the heapq calls of merge on iter_heap, where tuple comparison runs __eq__ (accepted there); no other comparison, dict key or membership test has a _KeyIter operand
default reject asyncstdlib._lrucache.LRUAsyncBoundCallable.__getattr__: initialized slots and normal methods do not fail on lookup; missing forwarded names and AttributeError from admitted metadata descriptors reach fallback at the explicitly accepted sites142,171,175,179,183. Generic callable roles admit no package value (header)
default reject asyncstdlib.functools.AwaitableValue.__await__, asyncstdlib.functools._FutureCachedPropertyValue.__await__: only an await on the value of a cached_property attribute runs these, and the package awaits one only in _FutureCachedPropertyValue._await_impl (accepted there); every other await is of a coroutine, of what __anext__, aclose or athrow return, or of a client awaitable (the awaitable role admits no package value, header)
default reject asyncstdlib._typing.SupportsBool.__bool__, asyncstdlib._typing.SupportsLT.__lt__, asyncstdlib._typing.SupportsAdd.__add__, asyncstdlib._typing.ACloseable.aclose: methods of typing.Protocol classes that no package class subclasses; a Protocol is not instantiated (scope rule B1), so these bodies never run
default reject asyncstdlib.functools.CachedProperty.__get__, asyncstdlib.functools.CachedProperty.__set_name__, asyncstdlib._lrucache.LRUAsyncCallable.__get__, asyncstdlib._lrucache.LRUAsyncBoundCallable.__get__: no package class body binds a CachedProperty, an LRU cache or a bound LRU cache, so no class statement or attribute access of the package reaches these descriptor methods; they run on client classes (CachedProperty.__get__ is accepted at the getattr() of _instance_value)

